---
description: Bash style for dmp-root, its libraries and install.sh
globs: ["scripts/**", "install.sh"]
---

# Shell scripts

- `#!/usr/bin/env bash` and `set -euo pipefail` in entry points; libraries in
  `scripts/lib/` start with `# shellcheck shell=bash` and only define functions.
- Function names start with `dmp_`. Log with `dmp_step`, `dmp_ok`, `dmp_warn`,
  `dmp_error`; exit with `dmp_die` (1, operation failed) or `dmp_usage_error`
  (2, bad input).
- Quote every expansion. Use arrays for argument lists. No `eval`, no
  `source` of anything but the shipped libraries.
- Replace files atomically: write a temp file in the same folder, then `mv`.
  Keep the previous version when a later check (configtest) can still fail.
- Private keys are created 0600 before they are written to.
- Check that a file is the panel's before changing it (`dmp_vhost_require_managed`,
  the hosts block markers); refuse with exit 1 and leave it as is otherwise.
- Under `set -e`, a final `cond && cmd` returns 1 when `cond` is false and can
  end the script; use `if` for anything that is not the last word.
- `shellcheck -x` must pass with no warnings (`wpcore` is a verbatim copy and is
  checked at error level only).
- Every `dmp-root` command has bats coverage in `scripts/tests/`, running against
  `setup_tree` with stubbed `a2ensite`, `apache2ctl`, `systemctl` and friends.
- `!` before a command does not fail a bats test; assert with `[ ... ]` or
  `run` and check `$status`.
